<title>SINGAPORE: Bank Indosuez leads financing China deal.</title>
<headline>Bank Indosuez leads financing China deal.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Indosuez said on Tuesday it would be the agent and lead arranger in the financing of a US$337 million power project in China.  </p>
<p>The syndicate of international banks includes Korea Development Bank (KDB) and JP Morgan, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The loan agreement is for the U.S. dollar financing of a coal-fired power plant at Jingyuan in Gansu province. The plant, which is 50 percent complete, is scheduled to be ready in October 1997.</p>
<p>Banque Indosuez said the project will be 25 percent financed by equity with total debt financing amounting to US$253 million provided in renminbi by the State Development Bank and China Construction Bank and in U.S. dollars by a syndicate of  </p>
<p>international banks led by Banque Indosuez, KDB and JP Morgan.</p>
<p>The project is a joint venture between the State Development Investment Corporation of Beijing, Gansu provincial entities and a foreign investment vehicle owned by CEA -- a member of New Jersey utility group, PSEG -- and the Asian Infrastructure Fund. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
